Catapult `catapult-openfield-connect-pp-cli` gotchas, all verified live 2026-06-10:

- `statistics` flags `--parameters`, `--group-by`, `--filters` each take JSON
  (array / array / array-of-objects: `{"name","comparison","values"}`).
- The `date` filter is **silently ignored upstream** — full athlete history comes
  back regardless. Pull everything, filter client-side.
- Baylor account parameter quirk: display name "PL_High (Avg)" sits on slug
  `pl_med_(avg)` but returns HIGH-band values (== `pl_high` on all 544 Tezino
  sessions). Slug is a fossil of a pre-rename calc; the data is correct.
- PL bands sum to total: pl_low + pl_med + pl_high + pl_veryhigh ~= total_player_load.
  `high_load` ("High Player Load") = med + high + veryhigh composite.
- At single-athlete per-activity granularity, every "(Avg)" parameter equals its
  base parameter; they only diverge in squad-level queries.
- Tezino athlete ID: `7a8e8546-4e0f-47df-979e-11694f73e70c`.

**Why:** these cost real debugging time and are invisible in the CLI docs.
**How to apply:** any future statistics pull — use JSON flags, ignore date filters,
trust pl_med_(avg) as high-band. Working reference: `scripts/extract_tezino_gps.py`.
